  {"date": "2013-07-05", "venue": "Saratoga Performing Arts Center", "city": "Saratoga Springs", "state": "NY", "gap": 1599, "set": "2", "note": "Phish debut.", "out": ">", "nb": 1, "xprev": "David Bowie", "next": "Light"},
  {"date": "2013-07-17", "venue": "Verizon Wireless Amphitheatre at Encore Park", "city": "Alpharetta", "state": "GA", "gap": 8, "set": "2", "note": "Fish on the Marimba Lumina.", "out": "->", "nb": 1, "prev": "Water in the Sky", "in": ">", "next": "Fluffhead"},
  {"date": "2013-07-21", "venue": "FirstMerit Bank Pavilion at Northerly Island", "city": "Chicago", "state": "IL", "gap": 3, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "The third appearance of \"Energy\" opens a rather (in)famous set and is the longest version so far. A bit of banter about the crowd sticking around in the rain finally gives way to the song. The jam begins and is a ball of frenzied, well, energy. The band locks in, Trey and Page have some great interplay. The frenzy eventually gives way to a spacey ending, replete with some of Mike's famous \"bass bombs\" and eventually > into \"Ghost\".", "out": ">", "nb": 1, "xprev": "Run Like an Antelope", "next": "Ghost"},
  {"date": "2013-08-04", "venue": "Bill Graham Civic Auditorium", "city": "San Francisco", "state": "CA", "gap": 8, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "This version opens the second set, where the song is most commonly found. The jam stays mostly in the bounds of the song until it turns on a dime to a Fish-led jam, accented by excellent play from the rest of the band. > an excellent \"Runaway Jim\".", "out": ">", "nb": 1, "xprev": "Pebbles and Marbles", "next": "Runaway Jim"},
  {"date": "2019-07-09", "venue": "Mohegan Sun Arena", "city": "Uncasville", "state": "CT", "gap": 226, "set": "1", "out": "->", "nb": 1, "first": 1, "next": "Weekapaug Groove"},
  {"date": "2019-12-08", "venue": "North Charleston Coliseum", "city": "North Charleston", "state": "SC", "gap": 15, "set": "2", "out": "->", "nb": 1, "prev": "Stealing Time From the Faulty Plan", "in": ">", "next": "Soul Planet"},
  {"date": "2020-02-22", "venue": "Moon Palace", "city": "Cancun", "state": "Quintana Roo", "gap": 7, "set": "2", "out": ">", "nb": 1, "xprev": "Twist", "next": "Soul Planet"},
  {"date": "2021-10-20", "venue": "Matthew Knight Arena", "city": "Eugene", "state": "OR", "gap": 28, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Significantly more accomplished than its short 12:45 time stamp would suggest. The jam shifts at 6:00 to D in various modes, then to F bliss at 7:45. This yields a smooth and linear growth to a predictable but satisfying peak around 11 minutes in. The final minute wrangles down to quiet and introspective space.", "out": "->", "nb": 1, "prev": "Mr. Completely", "next": "Timber (Jerry the Mule)"},
  {"date": "2022-08-14", "venue": "Alpine Valley Music Theatre", "city": "East Troy", "state": "WI", "gap": 47, "set": "2", "out": ">", "nb": 1, "xprev": "Everything's Right", "next": "Gotta Jibboo"},
  {"date": "2023-08-02", "venue": "Madison Square Garden", "city": "New York", "state": "NY", "gap": 37, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "In from an excellent \"Axilla (II)\" outro, Trey orchestrates more conventional jamming, spritely soloing over Page's great piano play. A cool theme emerges after the 4:30 mark, which the band is content to explore, weaving in an array of different textures and sounds; this leads to confident, if not quite conventional improv, a fun jam that undoubtedly energizes a surprisingly musical -> and standout \"Meatstick.\"", "out": "->", "nb": 1, "prev": "Axilla (Part II)", "in": ">", "next": "Meatstick"},
